  "prediction": "**Groundbreaking Surgery Gives Boy Born Without Ears a New Lease on Life**\n\nNine-year-old Kieran Sorkin, born without ears, has undergone a pioneering procedure at Great Ormond Street Hospital in London. The surgery, which involved creating a pair of ears from Kieran's own ribs, has given the boy a new sense of confidence and self-esteem.\n\nKieran, who was born with bilateral microtia, a rare condition affecting one in 100,000 babies, had been struggling with his appearance and feeling self-conscious about his differences. However, thanks to the surgery, he can now hear and see himself with a new pair of ears.\n\nThe procedure, led by consultant plastic surgeon Neil Bulstrode, involved harvesting cartilage from Kieran's ribs and shaping it into ear frameworks. These frameworks were then inserted into pockets in the skin and shaped using suction to create a natural-looking ear.\n\nThe surgery, which took six hours to complete, has brought significant psychological benefits to Kieran. His father, David Sorkin, said that the boy's confidence has improved exponentially, and he is now able to interact with his peers without feeling self-conscious about his appearance.\n\nThe surgery is not only a cosmetic procedure but also has a significant impact on Kieran's quality of life. Bulstrode said that the surgery brings a \"huge boost\" to patients with microtia, improving their confidence and performance at school.\n\nGreat Ormond Street Hospital performs around 40 of these operations each year, although most are to create one missing ear. The hospital is also working on developing new techniques for ear reconstruction using stem cells, which could potentially be less invasive than the current method.\n\nKieran's surgery is a testament to the advancements in medical technology and the dedication of medical professionals who are working tirelessly to improve the lives of children born with rare conditions. As Kieran's father said, \"We could not have wished for a better result.\"\n\n**Key Statistics:**\n\n* 1 in 100,000 babies are born with bilateral microtia\n* Great Ormond Street Hospital performs around 40 ear reconstruction surgeries each year\n* The surgery takes around 6 hours to complete\n* Kieran will need a second operation in six months to make his ears stand out from the scalp more\n\n**Future Developments:**\n\n* Researchers at Great Ormond Street Hospital are working on developing new techniques for ear reconstruction using stem cells\n* The new technique could potentially be less invasive than the current method\n* Scientists are also exploring the use of 3",
